From 6eb22f6856a99de965bbe24dc03f76a050401bc4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: leonieziechmann <48921293+leonieziechmann@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 21:50:19 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 14/15] perf(data): a smaller root import (Q2: at most +1 ms)

The maintainer's decision on Q2: the package import of an invoice without
data may grow by at most 1 ms against 0.6.0. Every line the import parses
costs about 10 k instructions (a comment line about 5 k, a closure about
25 k), so the eagerly parsed files say less and run less:

- invoice(): the re-entry hook passes only the design and issuer
  parameters to hydrate(..) (the skeleton's document values are samples
  and were never read), and the check for the applied marker moved into
  the lazy hydrate.typ; tools/contract/signature.py checks exactly that
  every design and issuer parameter is passed;
- the facades public/data.typ and public/payment.typ keep the signatures
  with a short doc comment and the `/// -> type` line of every function
  and parameter; the full docs moved next to the bodies (contract/api.typ,
  components/payment.typ), which load only when called;
- root: one lazy call for the coverage issues and the strict stop of a
  hydrated invoice; the items slot filters the marker frames once, and
  its panic text lives in contract/rows.typ;
- shorter comments in the shared path and in the region files.

Measured with the prototype harness' bench/impcount.py (valgrind
cachegrind, --jobs 1, import-only documents, tree copies under four sets
of names of equal length): the import delta against 0.6.0 drops from
+3.81 M to +2.97 M instructions on Typst 0.15.1 (+0.74 % to +0.58 % of
the import) and from +3.90 M to +3.11 M on 0.14.2 (+0.81 % to +0.65 %);
at the import's own untraced rate on the measuring VM (113.5 ms and
121.1 ms for the import) that is 0.84 to 0.65 ms and 0.99 to 0.79 ms.

